otal":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nNot reproducible in v4.3.stable.mono.official [77dcf97d8], v4.4.dev1.mono.official [28a72fa43], v4.4.dev3.mono.official [f4af8201b]\r\nProducible in v4.4.dev4.mono.official [36e6207bb]\r\nI was not able to get VR to work at all on v4.4.dev2.mono.official [97ef3c837], it would hang on the Godot splash. \n\n### System information\n\nWindows 11 - Godot 4.4 dev4 mono - Vulkan (Forward+) - AMD Ryzen 7 3800x - NVIDIA RTX 3070 Ti with driver 566.03\n\n### Issue description\n\nThe sky is not visible for the right eye in VR. (4.4.dev4)\r\n![Screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a6c17090-13d7-48a7-8159-4aa479cb708d)\r\nThe sky should be visible for both eyes. (4.4.dev3)\r\n![Screenshot](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/63fa8a0b-1cb3-4bbd-94e5-0927ad5f271b)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create and open a new project\r\n2. Enable OpenXR and XR shaders\r\n3. Create a new scene with a WorldEnvironment with Background set to Sky and set a new material for the sky. I used a PhysicalSkyMaterial.\r\n4. Create an XROrigin node, and a XRCamera as a child\r\n5. Attach a script to the scene root that enables XR for the viewport\r\n```gdscript\r\nextends Node3D\r\nfunc _ready() -> void:\r\n\tget_viewport().use_xr = true\r\n```\r\n6. Run the project\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[skyrepro.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/17738256/skyrepro.zip)\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://